/-
Weak: **THEOREM 2, STAGE 2 / certificate (p-stk), RELOAD NEGATIVE CERTIFICATE, COMPUTATION
HALF** — a concrete graph on which hart A's row is a family row ENDING RIGHT AFTER A RELOAD THAT
READ A WRONG VALUE: A (0, proc[0]) runs from allocproc + 0x38 into push_off's FIRST `mycpu()`
call, spills `ra = push_off + 0x14` (`sd ra, 8(sp)` at `S − 72 = 0x8000b398`, row item 6) and
`s0` (item 7); the racer C (2), a hand node holding nothing, stores `push_off + 0x30` (push_off's
OTHER mycpu return site) into that spill slot (`sd` 8 bytes, A's PRIVATE stack); mycpu's
`ld ra, 8(sp)` (item 8 = `rlKr .poMy1 q`) reads C's value, so the row — ended right after the
reload, `LEN = 9 = rlPos .poMy1 q` — is a `.poMy1` RELOAD CUT (`rlCutAt`, `reloadMis`, hence
`t2Cut A`).  B (1) is a phantom (empty row).  The reductio through `allocpidOpen2` (conjunct 1
`¬ t2Cut A`) that makes C's `HwpC` unprovable at `protXv6` (stack window private) is
`AxSpinT2q4`.

Lean-only (no Rocq source).  Design `notes/weak-lb-thm2-pins.md` §P1 ("(p-stk)", Q-P1-4), the
row-integrity analogue of (p-lk) (`AxSpinT2p2*`, `AxSpinT2q3`).  Modules: `AxSpinT2p3` (this:
racer, literal, graph, premises, the cut), `AxSpinT2p3a` (A's drive + the concrete graph and
premise bundle).  CHOICE OF RELOAD: `.poMy1` is the cheapest (9 events: acquire's 3 spills,
push_off's 3, mycpu's 2, the reload); every other reload lies past push_off's `noff` read
(`AxSpinT2f.rlPosGe`).

## `AllocPins2` for A (P1 finish, 2026-10-09)

The INTERIM field `rlEnd` (which excluded every reload-cut row) is DELETED from `AllocPins2`
(AxSpinT2f §5), so A's pins are now the three kept fields: **`pinsAS : AllocPins2 (gtAdGd (gTS E))
0 q0 := ⟨npNowrapAS E, npNcollAS E, ppArmAS E⟩`** (each vacuous: the nextpid / pop_off reads lie
past the row end).  (Formerly `notPinsAS : ¬ AllocPins2 …`, the honest report that the interim
premise excluded this row; `PROGRESS-AxSpinT2p3.md`.)  B's `AllocPins2` (empty row): `pinsBS`.

## What this file proves

§1 THE RACER: `rapaX` (A's mycpu `ra` spill slot, `sZ 0 − 72`, RAM), `wX = ppo 0x30`, `rcMS`
(`sd wX, 0(rapaX); hlt`), `rcRowS` (its 1-item row), `rcRunS` (its run: 1 step, row consumed).
§2 THE LITERAL: `encAS`/`rowAS` (A's 9 items = (p-lk)'s / (a′)'s first 8 — acquire's and
push_off's and mycpu's spills, values the entry registers' — then the reload of `rapaX` reading
`wX` at timestamp 8 = C's store; checked by `rowsFixedS`), `rowsS = [rowAS, [], rcRowS]`, `ilS`
(A's 0..6, C's store, A's 7, 8), `q0 = ⟨true, false, 0, false⟩` (`AxSpinT2c1.q0`), `sizesS`
(`rowAS.length = 9 = rlPos .poMy1 q0`).
§3 THE GRAPH: `gTS E = graphOfSc img rowsS ilS E`, `growAS/BS/CS` (`HrowC`), `shilS`, `emsCS`
+ `okCS`, `okBS`, `gRS`/`gtGEqS`.
§4 PREMISES, at every emission `E`:
  `preAS : allocPre (grow (gtAdGd (gTS E)) 0) q0 0 (sZ 0) (pEx 0)` (no gate is passed: every
    panic cut is ≥ 32, every other reload cut ≥ 11);
  THE SPILL / RELOAD FACTS: `spillLitS` (item 6 writes `stBytes 8 (ppo 0x14)` at `rapaX` — the
    spill is right), `reloadLitS` (item 8 reads `rapaX`, value `wbytes 8 wX`), `misLitS`
    (`wbytes 8 wX ≠ stBytes 8 (ppo 0x14)`), `rfAS` (A's reload sources C's store `(2, 0)`);
  THE CUT: `gateAS : ¬ rlEndOk .poMy1 (grow …) q0` (the ROW-END gate, = `rlGateOk` at
    `.poMy1`), `rlCutAS : rlCutAt (grow …) q0`,
    **`misAS : reloadMis (gtAdGd (gTS E)) 0 (sZ 0) (pEx 0)`**, **`cutAS : t2Cut …`** (via
    `AxSpinT2f.reloadCut`), `cutAtAS : t2CutAt (grow …) q0 0`; it is NO panic / `intr_on` cut
    (`notPanicAS`, `notIntrAS`, for every family parameters); `notCompleteAS`;
  A's pins: `npNowrapAS`, `npNcollAS`, `ppArmAS`, bundled as `pinsAS : AllocPins2 …`;
  phantom B: `preBS`, `pinsBS`, `notCutBS`, `notCompleteBS`;
  `honestAS`, `textFixedS` (h < 3), `imgNoffS` (`HimgNoff`), `imgClbS` (`Himgc`), `imgNpS`
  (`Himgn`, n0 = 1), `hartsS`.

## Pins / honesty
* The literal was GENERATED by hand from (p-lk)'s literal (`AxSpinT2p2.encA2`, whose first 8
  items are A's spills, values from the entry registers, independent of the racer); the reload's
  value / timestamp are C's.  `rowsFixedS` re-checks it against `sim`; the run premise is
  `drive2`'s (AxSpinT2p3a: the REAL `riscvStep` on this row — the reload loads `wX` into `ra`).
* C is a hand node (no fetch/decode — not graph events under Stage C); its emission `emsCS` is
  hand-written (a constant store: no register sources).  C's target is A's stack (`sZ 0 − 72`),
  the window `protXv6` keeps private — the reductio (later) refutes C's WPd there.
* The row ends right after the reload: A has NOT yet executed mycpu's `ret` (the diverted
  return is the continuation the family excludes / refutes, design §P1).
* Inherited (a′) scope (AxSpinT2pt / AxSpinT2c1 headers).  `q0` is a choice (`b` is not fixed by
  a 9-item prefix; `t2Cut` quantifies `q` itself).

Reused: `AxSpinT2p1.*` (checkers `preB`/`pins2B`/`offCutsB`, `growOf`, `rowAt`, `notCompleteNil`,
`himgNoff`), `AxSpinT2c1.img`/`dec`/`q0`/`sZ`/`hartOkB`/`valAt`/`gvRow`, `AxSpinT2c5.readsOffB`/
`imgAgree`/`imgClb`/`imgNp`/`σX`, `stv`/`hp`/`zeroRegs`/`nrunWrite`/`hlt` (AxSpinX3/X4,
AxClsStep2), `AxSpinPO.ppo`, `rlCutAt`/`reloadMis`/`t2Cut`/`AllocPins2`/`notCutOfLen`/
`AxSpinT2f.reloadCut`/`notCutOfComplete`/`cutPosGe`/`kEqs`/`rlEndOk`/`rlEndExp` (AxSpinT2f), `grfAtBSpec`
(AxGraphDec).  Names: Lean-only, `Weak.AxSpinT2p3.*` (grepped absent).
-/
import Weak.AxSpinT2p1
import Weak.AxSpinT2d

namespace Weak

open Iris Iris.BI Iris.ProofMode Iris.Std MachCSL MachCSL.Stdpp
open Sail Sail.ConcurrencyInterfaceV1
open LeanRV64D LeanRV64D.Functions
open AxSpinT2pt
open AxSpinT2c1 (img dec q0 sZ hartOkB)

namespace AxSpinT2p3

/-! # 1. The racer C: a wrong return address in A's spill slot -/

/-- A's mycpu `ra` spill slot (`sZ 0 − 72 = 0x8000b398`, A's stack) as a physical address. -/
def rapaX : PAddr := zPa 0x8000b398

theorem rapaXRam : devAddr rapaX = false := by decide +kernel
theorem rapaXZ : paZ rapaX = sZ 0 - 72 := by decide +kernel

/-- The planted value: push_off's OTHER mycpu return site (`push_off + 0x30`). -/
def wX : BitVec 64 := AxSpinPO.ppo 0x30

/-- THE RACER: `sd wX, 0(rapaX)` — a store into A's private stack, no ownership. -/
abbrev rcMS : SailM Unit := stv 8 rapaX wX hlt

/-- C's row: the one plain store. -/
def rcRowS : List Lbl := [.LStore false (paZ rapaX) (WeakInterpProj.wbytes 8 wX) .WCplain]

/-- C's run on its row (1 step, row consumed). -/
theorem rcRunS (cpu : CPU) (GD : Gdexec) (i : Agent) (Hrow : AxOpsem.grow GD i = rcRowS) :
    nsteps (astepAnyNfGv GD i) 1 ⟨hp cpu rcMS zeroRegs, 0⟩ ⟨hp cpu hlt zeroRegs, 1⟩ :=
  nsteps_l (nrunWrite cpu GD i 8 (by decide) rapaX rapaXRam wX hlt zeroRegs 0 .WCplain
    (by rw [Hrow]; rfl)) (nsteps_O _)

/-! # 2. The literal -/

/-- A's row (encoded; `AxSpinT2c1.dec`): the 8 spills, then mycpu's `ld ra` reading C's `wX`. -/
def encAS : List (Nat × Int × Nat × Nat × Nat) := [
  (1, 0x8000b3d8, 8, 0x80001bb6, 0), (1, 0x8000b3d0, 8, 0x8000b400, 0), (1, 0x8000b3c8, 8, 0x80012930, 0),
  (1, 0x8000b3b8, 8, 0x80000c68, 0), (1, 0x8000b3b0, 8, 0x8000b3e0, 0), (1, 0x8000b3a8, 8, 0x80012500, 0),
  (1, 0x8000b398, 8, 0x80000c32, 0), (1, 0x8000b390, 8, 0x8000b3c0, 0), (0, 0x8000b398, 8, 0x80000c4e, 8)]

def rowAS : List Lbl := encAS.map dec

/-- THE ROWS (harts 0, 1, 2 = A, phantom B, racer C). -/
def rowsS : List (List Lbl) := [rowAS, [], rcRowS]

/-- THE INTERLEAVING: A's 7 spills, C's store, A's `s0` spill and the reload. -/
def ilS : List Geid := (List.range 7).map (fun k => (0, k)) ++ [(2, 0), (0, 7), (0, 8)]

theorem sizesS : rowAS.length = 9 ∧ ilS.length = 10 ∧ rowAS.length = rlPos .poMy1 q0 := by
  decide +kernel

/-! # 3. The graph -/

/-- THE (p-stk) GRAPH, for any emission. -/
def gTS (E : List (List Eitem)) : GdexecT := graphOfSc img rowsS ilS E

theorem rowsFixedS : scProg rowsS (sim img rowsS ilS).sOut = rowsS := by decide +kernel

theorem growRS (E : List (List Eitem)) (h : Nat) :
    AxOpsem.grow (gtAdGd (gTS E)) h = AxSpinT2p1.rowAt rowsS h :=
  AxSpinT2p1.growOf rowsS ilS E h rowsFixedS

theorem growAS (E : List (List Eitem)) : AxOpsem.grow (gtAdGd (gTS E)) 0 = rowAS := growRS E 0
theorem growBS (E : List (List Eitem)) : AxOpsem.grow (gtAdGd (gTS E)) 1 = [] := growRS E 1
/-- `HrowC`: C's row is the racer's. -/
theorem growCS (E : List (List Eitem)) : AxOpsem.grow (gtAdGd (gTS E)) 2 = rcRowS := growRS E 2

theorem shilS : (shapesOkB rowsS && ilOkB rowsS ilS) = true := by decide +kernel

/-- C's emission (by hand): the constant store (no data / address register sources). -/
def emsCS : List Eitem := [(.LStore false (paZ rapaX) [] [] [], some 0)]

theorem okCS : hartOkB rowsS 2 emsCS = true := by decide +kernel

/-- The phantom B's (empty) emission check. -/
theorem okBS : hartOkB rowsS 1 [] = true := by decide +kernel

/-- The untagged graph. -/
def gRS : Gexec := ⟨fun a => some (img a), rowsS, ilS⟩

theorem gtGEqS (E : List (List Eitem)) : (gTS E).gtG = gRS := by
  show (⟨fun a => some (img a), scProg rowsS (sim img rowsS ilS).sOut, ilS⟩ : Gexec) = gRS
  rw [rowsFixedS]; rfl

/-! # 4. A's stage-2 premises and THE CUT -/

theorem preLitS : AxSpinT2p1.preB rowAS q0 0 (sZ 0) (AxSpinT2a.pEx 0) = true ∧
    AxSpinT2p1.preB [] q0 1 (sZ 1) (AxSpinT2a.pEx 1) = true := by
  constructor <;> decide +kernel

theorem pinsLitS : AxSpinT2p1.pins2B [] q0 1 = true := by decide +kernel

theorem clsLitS : rowClsOkB rowAS = true := by decide +kernel

/-- A's spill (item 6, `sd ra, 8(sp)` in mycpu) wrote the RIGHT value, `push_off + 0x14`. -/
theorem spillLitS : rowAS[t2KPo + 3]? =
    some (.LStore false (paZ rapaX) (stBytes 8 (AxSpinPO.ppo 0x14)) .WCplain) := by
  decide +kernel

/-- A's reload (item 8 = `rlKr .poMy1 q0`, mycpu's `ld ra, 8(sp)`) read `rapaX`, value C's `wX`. -/
theorem reloadLitS : rlKr .poMy1 q0 = t2KPo + 5 ∧
    AxSpinT2f.rv rowAS (rlKr .poMy1 q0) = some (WeakInterpProj.wbytes 8 wX) ∧
    rowAS[rlKr .poMy1 q0]? =
      some (.LLoad false (paZ rapaX) (List.replicate 8 8) (WeakInterpProj.wbytes 8 wX)) := by
  refine ⟨rfl, ?_, ?_⟩ <;> decide +kernel

/-- … and that value is NOT the spill's. -/
theorem misLitS : WeakInterpProj.wbytes 8 wX ≠ stBytes 8 (AxSpinPO.ppo 0x14) := by
  decide +kernel

theorem offLitS : AxSpinT2p1.offCutsB 0 q0 = true := by decide +kernel

/-- The row is short: every read past item 8 is absent. -/
theorem valPastS (k : Nat) (hk : 9 ≤ k) : AxSpinT2c1.valAt rowAS k = none := by
  unfold AxSpinT2c1.valAt
  rw [List.getElem?_eq_none (by rw [sizesS.1]; exact hk)]
  rfl

section prem
variable (E : List (List Eitem))

/-- **`allocPre`** for A on the cut row (prefix shape, value conditions; no gate is passed). -/
theorem preAS : allocPre (AxOpsem.grow (gtAdGd (gTS E)) 0) q0 0 (sZ 0) (AxSpinT2a.pEx 0) := by
  rw [growAS]; exact AxSpinT2p1.preOfB _ _ _ _ _ preLitS.1

/-- **The `.poMy1` reload gate is FLIPPED** on A's row: mycpu's `ra` reload read C's `wX`. -/
theorem gateAS : ¬ rlEndOk .poMy1 (AxOpsem.grow (gtAdGd (gTS E)) 0) q0 := by
  rw [growAS]
  intro h
  have H := h rfl _ reloadLitS.2.1
  simp only [rlEndExp, rlExp, Option.some.injEq] at H
  exact misLitS H.symm

/-- A's row is a RELOAD CUT row (`LEN = rlPos .poMy1 q0`, gate failed). -/
theorem rlCutAS : rlCutAt (AxOpsem.grow (gtAdGd (gTS E)) 0) q0 :=
  ⟨.poMy1, by rw [growAS]; exact sizesS.2.2, gateAS E⟩

theorem cutAtAS : t2CutAt (AxOpsem.grow (gtAdGd (gTS E)) 0) q0 0 := Or.inr (rlCutAS E)

/-- **A reload read a WRONG value** (`reloadMis`). -/
theorem misAS : reloadMis (gtAdGd (gTS E)) 0 (sZ 0) (AxSpinT2a.pEx 0) := ⟨q0, preAS E, rlCutAS E⟩

/-- **`t2Cut A` HOLDS, via `reloadMis`.** -/
theorem cutAS : t2Cut (gtAdGd (gTS E)) 0 (sZ 0) (AxSpinT2a.pEx 0) := AxSpinT2f.reloadCut (misAS E)

/-- every panic / `intr_on` cut lies past the row end (for every parameters). -/
theorem lenNeCut (j : T2Cj) (q : T2Prm) :
    (AxOpsem.grow (gtAdGd (gTS E)) 0).length ≠ cutPos j q := by
  rw [growAS, sizesS.1]
  have h1 := AxSpinT2f.cutPosGe j q
  have h2 : 20 ≤ t2KHd q := by rw [(AxSpinT2f.kEqs q).1]; split <;> omega
  intro h; omega

/-- It is NOT a panic cut … -/
theorem notPanicAS : ¬ entersPanic (gtAdGd (gTS E)) 0 (sZ 0) (AxSpinT2a.pEx 0) :=
  fun ⟨q, j, _, _, hL, _⟩ => lenNeCut E j q hL

/-- … nor an `intr_on` cut: the cut is the reload's alone. -/
theorem notIntrAS : ¬ intrOnCut (gtAdGd (gTS E)) 0 (sZ 0) (AxSpinT2a.pEx 0) :=
  fun ⟨q, _, hL, _⟩ => lenNeCut E .ppI q hL

/-- A is not complete. -/
theorem notCompleteAS : ¬ t2Complete (gtAdGd (gTS E)) 0 (sZ 0) (AxSpinT2a.pEx 0) :=
  fun hc => AxSpinT2f.notCutOfComplete hc (cutAS E)

/-- `rowClsHonest` for A. -/
theorem honestAS : rowClsHonest (AxOpsem.grow (gtAdGd (gTS E)) 0) := by
  rw [growAS]; exact rowClsHonestOfB _ clsLitS

/-- A's reload sources C's store `(C, 0)`. -/
theorem rfLitS : grfAtB gRS (paZ rapaX) (2, 0) (0, rlKr .poMy1 q0) = true := by decide +kernel

theorem rfAS : grfAt (gtAdGd (gTS E)).gdG (paZ rapaX) (2, 0) (0, rlKr .poMy1 q0) := by
  show grfAt (gTS E).gtG _ _ _
  rw [gtGEqS]
  exact (grfAtBSpec _ _ _ _).1 rfLitS

/-! ## A's guarded pins (header "`AllocPins2` for A") -/

/-- `AllocPins2.npNowrap` for A (vacuous: the nextpid read is past the row end). -/
theorem npNowrapAS : ∀ vs, graphValue (gtAdGd (gTS E)) (0, t2KBd q0) = some vs →
    (wordOfBytes 4 vs : BitVec 32) ≠ 1000#32 ∧ (wordOfBytes 4 vs : BitVec 32).toNat + 1 < 2 ^ 32 := by
  intro vs hv
  rw [AxSpinT2c1.gvRow, growAS, valPastS _ (by decide)] at hv
  cases hv

/-- `AllocPins2.npNcoll` for A (vacuous). -/
theorem npNcollAS : ∀ vs, graphValue (gtAdGd (gTS E)) (0, t2KBd q0) = some vs → ∀ j, j < 64 →
    ∀ v, graphValue (gtAdGd (gTS E)) (0, t2KBd q0 + 1 + j) = some v →
      (wordOfBytes 4 v : BitVec 32) ≠ wordOfBytes 4 vs := by
  intro vs hv
  rw [AxSpinT2c1.gvRow, growAS, valPastS _ (by decide)] at hv
  cases hv

/-- `AllocPins2.ppArm` for A (vacuous: pop_off's read is past the row end). -/
theorem ppArmAS : ∀ vn, graphValue (gtAdGd (gTS E)) (0, t2KPp q0 + 6) = some vn →
    (addiwm1 (ldRes false 4 vn) != zero_reg) = q0.c := by
  intro vn hv
  rw [AxSpinT2c1.gvRow, growAS, valPastS _ (by decide)] at hv
  cases hv

/-- **`AllocPins2`** for A (the three kept fields; P1: no row-end reload premise any more). -/
theorem pinsAS : AllocPins2 (gtAdGd (gTS E)) 0 q0 := ⟨npNowrapAS E, npNcollAS E, ppArmAS E⟩

/-! ## The phantom B (empty row) -/

theorem preBS : allocPre (AxOpsem.grow (gtAdGd (gTS E)) 1) q0 1 (sZ 1) (AxSpinT2a.pEx 1) := by
  rw [growBS]; exact AxSpinT2p1.preOfB _ _ _ _ _ preLitS.2

theorem pinsBS : AllocPins2 (gtAdGd (gTS E)) 1 q0 := by
  apply AxSpinT2p1.pins2OfB; rw [growBS]; exact pinsLitS

theorem notCutBS : ¬ t2Cut (gtAdGd (gTS E)) 1 (sZ 1) (AxSpinT2a.pEx 1) :=
  notCutOfLen (preBS E) (by rw [growBS]; exact (AxSpinT2p1.offCutsOf offLitS).1)
    (by rw [growBS]; exact (AxSpinT2p1.offCutsOf offLitS).2)

theorem notCompleteBS : ¬ t2Complete (gtAdGd (gTS E)) 1 (sZ 1) (AxSpinT2a.pEx 1) :=
  AxSpinT2p1.notCompleteNil (growBS E)

/-! ## Image, text -/

theorem readsOffS : (List.range 3).all (fun h => AxSpinT2c5.readsOffB (AxSpinT2p1.rowAt rowsS h)) =
    true := by
  decide +kernel

/-- **`textFixed`** on the (p-stk) graph. -/
theorem textFixedS (h : Agent) (hh : h < 3) :
    textFixed (gtAdGd (gTS E)) h (imgS AxSpinT2c5.σX) := by
  refine ⟨fun a b hab => ?_, ?_⟩
  · have H := AxSpinT2c5.imgAgree [] a b hab
    rw [show (gtAdGd (AxSpinT2c1.gT3 [])).gdG.gxImg = fun a => some (img a) from rfl] at H
    rw [show (gtAdGd (gTS E)).gdG.gxImg = fun a => some (img a) from rfl]
    exact H
  intro k lb aq base n vs hk hr hi
  rw [growRS] at hk
  have H := List.all_eq_true.1 (List.all_eq_true.1 readsOffS h (List.mem_range.2 hh))
    lb (List.mem_of_getElem? hk)
  rw [hr] at H
  simp only [hi, Option.isNone_some] at H
  cases H

/-- `HimgNoff` on the (p-stk) graph. -/
theorem imgNoffS : HimgNoff (gtAdGd (gTS E)).gdG.gxImg 0 1 := AxSpinT2p1.himgNoff 0 1

/-- `Himgc` (`lk->cpu` = 0 in the image). -/
theorem imgClbS (L : Xlay) (hL : L.xlLk = AxSpinT2a.zLk) :
    ∀ a, a ∈ clb L → (gTS E).gtG.gxImg a = some b0 := by
  intro a ha
  have H := AxSpinT2c5.imgClb [] L hL a ha
  rw [show (AxSpinT2c1.gT3 []).gtG.gxImg = fun a => some (img a) from rfl] at H
  rw [show (gTS E).gtG.gxImg = fun a => some (img a) from rfl]
  exact H

/-- `Himgn` (nextpid = 1 in the image). -/
theorem imgNpS (L : Xlay) (hL : L.xlNp = AxSpinT2a.zNp) :
    ∀ (j : Nat) a v, (npb L)[j]? = some a →
      (WeakInterpProj.wbytes 4 (BitVec.ofInt 32 1))[j]? = some v → (gTS E).gtG.gxImg a = some v := by
  intro j a v h1 h2
  have H := AxSpinT2c5.imgNp [] L hL j a v h1 h2
  rw [show (AxSpinT2c1.gT3 []).gtG.gxImg = fun a => some (img a) from rfl] at H
  rw [show (gTS E).gtG.gxImg = fun a => some (img a) from rfl]
  exact H

/-- Only harts 0 and 2 emit memory events (1 is a phantom). -/
theorem hartsS : ∀ e, e ∈ (gTS E).gtG.gxGmo → e.1 ∈ [0, 1, 2] := by
  intro e he
  have H : ilS.all (fun e : Geid => decide (e.1 ∈ [0, 1, 2])) = true := by decide +kernel
  exact of_decide_eq_true (List.all_eq_true.1 H e he)

end prem

end AxSpinT2p3

end Weak
